      "id": "FRAME-ABI-MACRO",
      "priority": 0,
      "path": "lib/mem.h",
      "line": 76,
      "title": "Frame capacity macro overwrites the generated frame ABI reserve",
      "evidence": [
        "lib/mem.c includes gambit.h before mem.h",
        "include/_gambit/module_generation.h.in defines ___FRAME_RESERVE as 3",
        "mem.h redefines it as MAX_NB_FRAME_SLOTS+1+SUBTYPED_BODY",
        "FRAME_SPACE and FRAME_RETI_RA expand it at their later use sites"
      ],
      "impact": "A one-slot frame has generated span 4 and runtime span 8196 in the selected no-handle layout. Census/copy and generated frames disagree, or a redefinition warning becomes a build error.",
      "fixBoundary": "Give the capacity bound its own responsibility-specific identifier and preserve the configured frame ABI constant. Requalify all mem.h consumers under the original producer.",
      "negativeAcceptance": "Independently decoded generated frame strides must agree with runtime consumers after mem.h, including RETN, RETI, roots and restore. Existing fixtures synthesized solely with the runtime macro are insufficient."
    },
    {
      "id": "REST-WHOLE-BATCH",
      "priority": 1,
      "path": "lib/mem.h",
      "line": 75,
      "title": "New rest reserve omits the per-pair physical multiplier",
      "evidence": [
        "Rest and keyword-rest fallback still finish i pairs and allocate the full np vector without a preflight",
        "Selected pair size is 2 payload words plus PAIR_BODY 1",
        "MAX_NB_ARGS 8192 plus MAX_NB_PARMS 1024 plus vector header 1 plus one pair 3 is 9220",
        "An admitted suffix of 4000 pending pairs and np=1 writes 12002 words"
      ],
      "impact": "Increasing the fixed fudge still cannot authorize all supported rest batches before their first store or pop.",
      "fixBoundary": "Implement checked whole-batch interval admission and the typed refusal/retry roots from the DEV handoff. Preserve the original heap budget.",
      "negativeAcceptance": "Exact-fit and one-word-short ordinary and keyword-rest runs must witness zero fallback writes and pops on refusal, and intact roots through GC/retry."
    }
  ],
